      "narrative": "A patient began Velmoradine 20 mg once daily for essential hypertension on 3 March 2026. Nine days later she developed a widespread itchy maculopapular rash across the trunk and both forearms. The drug was withdrawn on 13 March and the rash began to settle within 48 hours. No corticosteroid was required. She had taken no other new medicine in the preceding month. The rash has now completely resolved and the patient has not been rechallenged.",
